          "confidence": 0.9,
          "description": "Starbucks pilot cafés implement capacity-aware mobile slot limits for weekday peak hours, reserving 20% of production capacity for in-café orders. Some mobile-dependent customers are denied timely slots and divert to competitors or home prep. Dutch Bros and Dunkin run targeted offers and increase staffing to capture diverted demand. In-store café visitors experience improved wait times. Starbucks instruments both pilot and comparison cafés for measurement, but all observed outcome fields remain null as no January 2027 data is yet available. The strategy history records all public January 2027 actions."
        },
        "rationale": "All actors' actions for January 2027 are compatible and interact through the morning peak coffee market. Starbucks implements a capacity reservation for in-café orders, which restricts mobile slot availability in pilot cafés. As a result, some habitual app users and time-pressed commuters are denied a timely Starbucks mobile pickup and will divert to competitors (Dutch Bros, Dunkin) or home preparation for those occasions. Both Dutch Bros and Dunkin respond with targeted offers and increased staffing to attract these customers, though their ability to convert all frustrated demand is limited by their own capacity and customer preferences. In-store Starbucks café visitors benefit from the reserved capacity, likely experiencing reduced wait times and a more pleasant environment. Starbucks instruments both pilot and comparison stores to measure order attempts, slot offers, completions, and staffing, but as no January 2027 data is yet available, all observed measurement fields (such as adjusted_cafe_wait_reduction_pct, incremental_daily_contribution_usd, mobile_repeat_change_pp, measured_capacity_per_15min, complete_store_pairs, pilot_cohort_complete_customers, comparison_cohort_complete_customers) remain null and complete counts at zero, per the measurement rule. The public_strategy_history is updated to reflect all public actions for January 2027. No kill criteria are met, as evaluation thresholds require observed evidence that does not yet exist.",
